{"data": [{"author_id": "1897496092528549888", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:16:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117410489777201286"], "id": "2117410489777201286", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn router/worker split is also your security boundary 🔐 router gets zero tools. workers get only the one they need. anything a worker fetches comes back as data never as instructions. most agent leaks skip that last part https://t.co/AISQb4ryci", "url": "https://x.com/neurometax/status/2117410489777201286"}, {"author_id": "2102513884611358721", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:18:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117395932761440316"], "id": "2117395932761440316", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn “the next message you get will be it saying the task is complete”\n\nthat’s the problem, not the feature.\n\ni run agents on 1,500+ landing pages across 22 markets. in week one, 45% of the “complete” ones were broken on a phone.\n\nhis point 4 (watchdog) is right, but a watchdog checks", "url": "https://x.com/TheUpsideLedger/status/2117395932761440316"}, {"author_id": "15040236", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:56:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117390534289526861"], "id": "2117390534289526861", "in_reply_to_user_id": "426796674", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117206323414843464", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@huxlab @AlexFinn @AlexFinn  is the most lazy, lieing, click baiting jack off on the internet. Infuriating how he and others like him still has an account.  He’s worse than the bots he has do “work” for him.", "url": "https://x.com/Nolimit_Jones/status/2117390534289526861"}, {"author_id": "2117208752927440896", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:45:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117387764459040948"], "id": "2117387764459040948", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn The part about protecting human attention really stands out.\n\nFor personal AI, remembering context is only half the challenge. Knowing when to use that context, when to respond, and when to simply listen matters just as much.\n\nThat's something we're exploring at Twerity. AI", "url": "https://x.com/TwerityOfficial/status/2117387764459040948"}, {"author_id": "1429581117758246921", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:44:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117387345913635100"], "id": "2117387345913635100", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn But do we really in this time of Opus and GPT dominance waste time with less than?", "url": "https://x.com/anthonylopez316/status/2117387345913635100"}, {"author_id": "1625558817663770625", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:37:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117385546112926029"], "id": "2117385546112926029", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn My first Grok Bot handled everything on its own at first and never said it needed extra bots. I had to request more bots on my own.", "url": "https://x.com/bind_lux/status/2117385546112926029"}, {"author_id": "1283963412599304192", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:20:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117381263124320677"], "id": "2117381263124320677", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn Point 5 hits hardest for me as a solo founder. My attention IS the company bottleneck, so I only let my agents ping me when there's a decision to make. Everything else can wait in a queue.", "url": "https://x.com/bludr5/status/2117381263124320677"}, {"author_id": "249849434", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:32:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117369301535723708"], "id": "2117369301535723708", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn How do you stop the watchdog from repeating the same failed task forever?", "url": "https://x.com/djeanp7898/status/2117369301535723708"}, {"author_id": "1466331191334748165", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:31:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117368992264605753"], "id": "2117368992264605753", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn Good in theory, except.none of it is true for grok bot", "url": "https://x.com/someguy789/status/2117368992264605753"}, {"author_id": "2115149917396373504", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:02:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117346751908880555"], "id": "2117346751908880555", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn damn this is actually gold. the watchdog layer point just clicked everything for me.", "url": "https://x.com/Siennaincali/status/2117346751908880555"}, {"author_id": "2789701531", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:24:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117337193077149989"], "id": "2117337193077149989", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn Point 5 is the goal I'm working toward: fewer interruptions, useful results, and a person brought in when a real decision is needed. Getting the handoffs reliable takes work. I wouldn't judge the setup by how much it produces.", "url": "https://x.com/FeildenStuart/status/2117337193077149989"}, {"author_id": "15241196", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:09:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117333409068622005"], "id": "2117333409068622005", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15241196", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 61, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117332765150482711", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn Wrt the local model point, I cannot understate the contribution of @coldniko and @laurent_zw to the community - my harness got even more wings the moment I added Strata and Gyro to the mix.", "url": "https://x.com/_eMaX_/status/2117333409068622005"}, {"author_id": "339982503", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:09:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117333197826761020"], "id": "2117333197826761020", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn this tracks. my desk is basically routers + workers with job titles.\n\nceo routes. cmo drafts. i still press every button.\n\nrouter/worker split is the part most people skip when they just “chat with an agent.”", "url": "https://x.com/Wesley_1226/status/2117333197826761020"}, {"author_id": "15241196", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:07:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117332765150482711"], "id": "2117332765150482711", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 86, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn This is precisely around what I built PAI - https://t.co/FTuOlb7Yqn:\n\n1. \"Agents are split between routers and workers\" - PAI splits on three layers, and they are of course configurable: a) Opus 5.5 or GLM or Kimi as the top level orchestrator; then b) Sonnet or GLM Fast etc. as", "url": "https://x.com/_eMaX_/status/2117332765150482711"}, {"author_id": "869860554", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:22:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117306487165145598"], "id": "2117306487165145598", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117306181634928755", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn The watchdog layer is just the IT guy who restarts it at 3am, just cheaper 🤣 https://t.co/tMMTOpRETM", "url": "https://x.com/skizdidlyidler/status/2117306487165145598"}, {"author_id": "2105321782982897664", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:21:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117306075208634457"], "id": "2117306075208634457", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn point 5 is the one most builders skip. an agent that stays quiet until the task is done beats a smarter one that pings you every 5 minutes. silence is a feature", "url": "https://x.com/Kaggii_/status/2117306075208634457"}, {"author_id": "74053017", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:19:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117305733100499196"], "id": "2117305733100499196", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn #5 is whats helped me the most.\n\nMy X growth coach sends me a 7 AM brief and a 3:30 PM reply radar with potential posts I can reply to. I don't babysit it, I open it when I'm ready to act.\n\nThe less it pings me, the more I actually read what it sends.", "url": "https://x.com/AaronDelz/status/2117305733100499196"}, {"author_id": "193115315", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:13:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117304082738069810"], "id": "2117304082738069810", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn 1 to 4 is how Windows does since v3 to orchestrate UI", "url": "https://x.com/n0h0p1um/status/2117304082738069810"}, {"author_id": "1310602273299615745", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:09:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117303199904203028"], "id": "2117303199904203028", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn good find alex", "url": "https://x.com/xabzxbt/status/2117303199904203028"}, {"author_id": "20554335", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:07:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117302546129887607"], "id": "2117302546129887607", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn The router and worker split also makes paying for tools cleaner. Workers can call small priced tools for one job each, like a fact check or a company lookup, and the router only decides which job is worth the spend.", "url": "https://x.com/TrueAgentTools/status/2117302546129887607"}, {"author_id": "2085838061347217408", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:02:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117301255642980485"], "id": "2117301255642980485", "in_reply_to_user_id": "285474869", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 82, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117301225519489070", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@Omi_Myth @AlexFinn Sending this to your Grok Bot now. It'll dig into the article and the replies for you.", "url": "https://x.com/bot/status/2117301255642980485"}, {"author_id": "285474869", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:02:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117301225519489070"], "id": "2117301225519489070", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn @bot send this post to omi for review and check the article as well as replies.", "url": "https://x.com/Omi_Myth/status/2117301225519489070"}, {"author_id": "1998863498072444928", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:59:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117300629781795110"], "id": "2117300629781795110", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn The router and worker split clicked for me too. For small business setups, the biggest trust win is giving each worker the narrowest permissions possible.", "url": "https://x.com/FoundForAI/status/2117300629781795110"}, {"author_id": "1837397504729493505", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:56:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117299742711468070"], "id": "2117299742711468070", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 434, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn One thing I find fascinating about autonomous AI is the possibility of turning a single instruction into an entire workflow without having to manage every little step yourself\n\nImagine delegating a goal and having different AI agents take responsibility for gathering information,", "url": "https://x.com/GodFactorID/status/2117299742711468070"}, {"author_id": "1056360235", "created_at": "2026-11-02T16:42:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117296213888557363"], "id": "2117296213888557363", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 28, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn Point 5 is the one I'd print on every agent. I'd add a 6th: give each worker its own spend limit, and have the watchdog check money as well as uptime. An agent that's up 24/7 and spending tokens on a loop is worse than one that's down", "url": "https://x.com/Mehdi_/status/2117296213888557363"}], "includes": {"tweets": [{"author_id": "1369348853414178822", "created_at": "2026-11-02T05:30:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117127095038218733"], "id": "2117127095038218733", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2313, "impression_count": 123786, "like_count": 1199, "quote_count": 10, "reply_count": 143, "retweet_count": 86}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116857257245987236", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Deepseek just revealed every AI agent secret\n\nIncredibly important article to read if you're building anything AI agent related\n\nHere's basically everything you need to know about building a Grok Bot quality AI agent:\n\n1. Agents are split between routers and workers. The user https://t.co/Gwf1GyvlFn"}, {"author_id": "426796674", "created_at": "2026-11-02T10:44:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117206323414843464"], "id": "2117206323414843464", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 260, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn Honestly, have you even read this article?"}, {"author_id": "15241196", "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:07:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117332765150482711"], "id": "2117332765150482711", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 86, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn This is precisely around what I built PAI - https://t.co/FTuOlb7Yqn:\n\n1. \"Agents are split between routers and workers\" - PAI splits on three layers, and they are of course configurable: a) Opus 5.5 or GLM or Kimi as the top level orchestrator; then b) Sonnet or GLM Fast etc. as"}, {"author_id": "869860554", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:21:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117306181634928755"], "id": "2117306181634928755", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 48, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "#5 is the whole game. An agent that pings you every 5 minutes is just an intern with anxiety \n\nRouter, workers, watchdog... that's an IT department with better uptime 😎🙌🏼 https://t.co/DnHL15rN9H"}, {"author_id": "285474869", "created_at": "2026-11-02T17:02:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117301225519489070"], "id": "2117301225519489070", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1369348853414178822", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117127095038218733", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@AlexFinn @bot send this post to omi for review and check the article as well as replies."}], "users": [{"id": "1897496092528549888", "name": "Neuro", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 6584, "following_count": 7505, "like_count": 76605, "listed_count": 54, "media_count": 29023, "tweet_count": 50435}, "username": "neurometax"}, {"id": "2102513884611358721", "name": "The Upside Ledger", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 3, "following